&Q000432 = A tigi to Suen for Ibbi-Suen (Ibbi-Suen A)
@composite
#project: etcslatf/inter
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.2.4.5.1
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.2.4.5.1&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

@div sa-gida A

A.1. en me sag₂!(GAN) nu-di i-lim u₅ men gal-la
#lem: en[lord]; me[Being]; sag[scatter]; di[speak]; ilim[radiance]; u[ride]; men[tiara]; gal[big]
#tr.en: Lord whose divine powers cannot be dispersed, who emits an awe-inspiring radiance, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.1

#etcsl#cite Cited in OB catalogue from Nibru (N3), 0.2.06, line 20

A.2. šul {d}suen ud ŋiš-he₂ e₃-a-še₃ {d}en-lil₂-le il₂-la
#lem: šul[youth]; Suen[1]DN; ud[sun]; ŋešhe[firmament]; e[leave]; Enlil[1]DN; il[raise]
#tr.en: great crown! Youthful @wDN{Suen}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.2

A.3. su-lim daŋal idim-e dirig {d}nin-lil₂-le tud-da
#lem: sulim[awesome radiance]; daŋal[wide]; idim[spring]; dirig[make more than]; Ninlil[1]DN; utud[give birth (to)]
#tr.en: light elevated by @wDN{Enlil} to shine forth in the firmament, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.3

A.4. diŋir muš₃-a-ni! UN-UN unken kur-kur-ra DU [...]
#lem: diŋir[deity]; muš[face]; X; unkin[assembly]; kur[mountain(s)]; X; X
#tr.en: wide-spreading majestic light, floating over the deep (?), born of @wDN{Ninlil}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.4

A.5. iti₆ X {d}i-bi₂-{d}suen-ŋu₁₀ X X X X mu-un-[...]
#lem: itud[moon]; X; Ibbisuen[1]RN; X; X; X; X; X
#tr.en: god whose appearance is ……, …… in the assembly of the lands! 
#etcsl: line-id=A.5

A.6. me nam-nun-na-ni an-da gu₂ la₂-[am₃]
#lem: me[Being]; namnun[magnificence]; an[sky]; gu[neck]; la[hang]
#tr.en: The moonlight ……, my @wRN{Ibbi-@wDN{Suen}}, ……. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.6

A.7. u₁₈-ru-ni giri₁₇-zal ki us₂-sa-[am₃]
#lem: urun[exalted]; kirizal[joy]; ki[place]; us[accompany]
#tr.en: His princely divine powers embrace the heavens; his …… is splendid, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.7

A.8. {d}dil-im₂-babbar-re {d}i-bi₂-{d}suen#-[ŋu₁₀]
#lem: Dilimbabbar[1]DN; Ibbisuen[1]RN
#tr.en: reaching the earth. @wDN{Ašimbabbar} ……, my @wRN{Ibbi-@wDN{Suen}}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.8

A.9. kalam-ma ku₆-ŋal₂-bi-še₃ uŋ₃ daŋal-la X [...]
#lem: kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; guŋal[inspector]; uŋ[people]; daŋal[wide]; X; X
#tr.en: to be canal inspector in the Land among the widespread people. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.9

A.10. {d}nanna men zid-da dalla mu-[X-e₃]
#lem: Nanna[1]DN; men[tiara]; zid[right]; dalla[(to be) bright]; e[leave]
#tr.en: @wDN{Nanna} has made the righteous crown shine forth radiantly. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.10

A.11. ŋidru ud du₆ ul-la {d}dil-im₂-babbar# [...]
#lem: ŋidru[scepter]; ud[sun]; u; ul[distant time]; Dilimbabbar[1]DN; X
#tr.en: @wDN{Ašimbabbar} has …… you the sceptre ……. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.11

## sandhi ud-du₆-ul-la < ud ula?

A.12. {d}i-bi₂-{d}suen-ŋu₁₀ uŋ₃ daŋal-la gu₂ X [...]
#lem: Ibbisuen[1]RN; uŋ[people]; daŋal[wide]; gu[neck]; X; X
#tr.en: My @wRN{Ibbi-@wDN{Suen}}, among the widespread people ……. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.12

A.13. ub-da an ki-ka kalam dug₃-ga ŋiri₃-na [...]
#lem: ub[corner]; an[sky]; ki[place]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; dug[good]; ŋiri[foot]; X
#tr.en: In the corners of heaven and earth, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.13

A.14. {d}nanna kur-kur-ra me-ni am₃-[...]
#lem: Nanna[1]DN; kur[mountain(s)]; me[Being]; X
#tr.en: in the beautiful land …… beneath his feet, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.14

A.15. an ki niŋ₂-daŋal-ba pa MU X X [...]
#lem: an[sky]; ki[place]; niŋdaŋala[vastness]; pa[branch]; X; X; X; X
#tr.en: @wDN{Nanna} has …… his divine powers in all lands; 
#etcsl: line-id=A.15

A.16. an-e nir GI-ba {d}aš-[im₂-babbar ...]
#lem: An[1]DN; nir[lordly]; X; Dilimbabbar[1]DN; X
#tr.en: he has …… widely in heaven and earth. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.16

A.17. {d}nanna nam-šul-la X hu-[...]
#lem: Nanna[1]DN; namšul[manhood]; X; X
#tr.en: @wDN{An} …… @wDN{Ašimbabbar} ……. @wDN{Nanna} has …… him in his youthfulness; 
#etcsl: line-id=A.17

A.18. ul-še₃ me ud til₃-la X X mu-ni-[...]
#lem: ul[distant time]; me[Being]; ud[sun]; til[live (of a single person)]; X; X; X
#tr.en: he has …… the divine powers of his lifetime forever. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.18

A.19. {d}i-<bi₂>-{d}suen-ŋu₁₀ X hu-mu-na-ni-[...]
#lem: Ibbisuen[1]RN; X; X
#tr.en: May he …… my @wRN{Ibbi-@wDN{Suen}}. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.19

A.20. dug₄-ga-ni u₁₈-ru gal sag₂ nu-di-dam
#lem: dug[speak]; urun[exalted]; gal[big]; sag[scatter]; di[speak]
#tr.en: @wDN{Nanna's} command is a great …… which cannot be dispersed. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.20

A.21. {d}i-bi₂-{d}suen šu mah-a-ni im-dab
#lem: Ibbisuen[1]RN; šu[hand]; mah[great]; dab[seize]
#tr.en: @wRN{Ibbi-@wDN{Suen}} has grasped his august hand; he has acted truthfully for him, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.21

A.22. zid-de₃-eš-še₃ mu-na-an-ak mu dug₃ sa₄-a-ni
#lem: zid[right]; ak[do]; mu[name]; dug[good]; še[call by name]
#tr.en: and so is named with a good name. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.22

@div trailer 

A.23. sa-gid₂-da-am₃
#lem: sagida[musical notation]
#tr.en: @fsux{Sa-gida}. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.23

@end trailer

@end sa-gida

@div sa-ŋara B

B.24. urim₂{ki} iri me nun šul {d}suen-na-kam
#lem: Urim[1]SN; iri[city]; me[Being]; nun[prince]; šul[youth]; Suen[1]DN
#tr.en: @wSN{Urim} is the city of youthful @wDN{Suen's} princely divine powers. 
#etcsl: line-id=B.24

B.25. an {d}en-lil₂ pap gal {d}nu-dim₂-mud
#lem: An[1]DN; Enlil[1]DN; pap[relation]; gal[big]; Nudimmud[1]DN
#tr.en: Let them give praise in a great song to @wDN{An}, 
#etcsl: line-id=B.25

B.26. ama {d}nin-tur₅ kalam-ma šir₃-ra-ni mah-am₃ me-teš₂ he₂-i-i
#lem: ama[mother]; Nintur[1]DN; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; šir[song]; mah[great]; meteš[praise]; e[bring out]
#tr.en: to @wDN{Enlil}, 
#etcsl: line-id=B.26

B.27. eš₃ urim₂{ki} iri me nun šul {d}suen-na-kam
#lem: eš[shrine]; Urim[1]SN; iri[city]; me[Being]; nun[prince]; šul[youth]; Suen[1]DN
#tr.en: to the eldest brother @wDN{Nudimmud} and to Mother @wDN{Nintur} of the Land. 
#etcsl: line-id=B.27

B.28. an {d}en-lil₂ pap gal {d}nu-dim₂-mud
#lem: An[1]DN; Enlil[1]DN; pap[relation]; gal[big]; Nudimmud[1]DN
#tr.en: The shrine @wSN{Urim} is the city of youthful @wDN{Suen's} princely divine powers. 
#etcsl: line-id=B.28

B.29. ama {d}nin-tur₅ kalam-ma šir₃-ra-ni mah-am₃ me-[teš₂] he₂-i-i
#lem: ama[mother]; Nintur[1]DN; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; šir[song]; mah[great]; meteš[praise]; e[bring out]
#tr.en: Let them give praise in a great song to @wDN{An}, 
#etcsl: line-id=B.29

B.30. {d}a-nun-na X X X X [...]
#lem: Anunak[1]DN; X; X; X; X; X
#tr.en: to @wDN{Enlil}, 
#etcsl: line-id=B.30

B.31. {d}en-ki [...]
#lem: Enkik[1]DN; X
#tr.en: to the eldest brother @wDN{Nudimmud} and to Mother @wDN{Nintur} of the Land. 
#etcsl: line-id=B.31

B.32. {d}X [...]
#lem: X[1]DN; X
#tr.en: The @wDN{Anuna} gods ……. @wDN{Enki} ……  
#etcsl: line-id=B.32

B.33. {d}[...]
#lem: X[1]DN
#tr.en: …… assembly where ……. …… festival (?) ……. 
#etcsl: line-id=B.33

B.34. {d}[...]
#lem: X[1]DN
#etcsl: line-id=B.34

B.35. unken ki X [...]
#lem: unkin[assembly]; ki[place]; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=B.35

B.36. EZEN X [...]
#lem: X; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=B.36

@div trailer 

B.37. sa-[ŋar]-ra-[am₃]
#lem: saŋara[musical notation]
#tr.en: @fsux{Sa-ŋara}. 
#etcsl: line-id=B.37

@end trailer

@end sa-ŋara

@div trailer 

B.38. tigi# {[d]}suen#-na-[kam]
#lem: tigi[drum or other musical instrument]; Suen[1]DN
#tr.en: A @fsux{tigi} of @wDN{Suen}. 
#etcsl: line-id=B.38

